    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "This problem can be broken down into smaller, more manageable parts. First, let's determine how many games a single team will have to play.\n\nEach team will play three games against each of the other eight teams. However, we have to be careful not to double count the games. Since the order in which the games are played does not matter, each game will be counted twice in our calculation. Thus, the total number of games can be calculated as follows:\n\n1. Each game is counted twice because the order of teams does not matter.\n2. Each team plays against 8 other teams, and they get to play 3 times per team.\n3. So, the formula to calculate the total number of games is: Total games = (Teams * Games per team / 2).\n\nPlugging in the values, we get:\n\nTotal games = (9*3/2) = 13.5",
